    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0638" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1902: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-14T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                                1928—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 12:48
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>118. Cumberland sailed for New York on March 12. We have read the greater part of
                    the excellent report which he has prepared and are in accord with his
                    recommendations. Before his departure he discussed his principal recommendation
                    briefly and informally <pb facs="0639" n="529" xml:id="pg529"/> with the
                    President, the Minister of Finance and General Moncada,<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d463-f1"/> all of whom expressed themselves as in complete accord
                    therewith.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d463-f1" n="68" xml:id="d463-f1-content">
                <p>Head of the Liberal Party.</p>
            </note>
